# Reach Creature::Dig's division with SkillLevel(SK_MINING) exactly 0 (bd inc-4ht).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dig-zero-skill.keys 1
#
# WHY A GNOME WARRIOR WITH WISDOM 3. SkillLevel(SK_MINING) (src/Create.cpp) has
# no floor of 1. For this character every term of it is known and they sum to
# zero:
#
#   ranks               0   Mining is never trained here
#   s_train            +2   Mining is a gnome race skill (lib/races.irh)
#   s_racial            0   the gnome template, alone among the five races that
#                           have Mining, carries no Stati[SKILL_BONUS,35]
#                           -- the kobold and dwarf templates both carry +2
#   s_kit              +2   the pickaxe is Mining's skill kit, SKILL_KIT_MOD +2
#   Mod2(min(WIS,STR)) -4   Mining takes the WORSE of Wisdom and Strength, and
#                           this character's Wisdom is 3
#
# Wisdom 3 comes from point buy ([p] on the attribute screen), which is why the
# stats below are typed rather than chosen from a rolled set: base Wisdom 5 plus
# the gnome's -2. Every other attribute is bought up because point buy will not
# release the character while a point is unspent.
#
# WHY THE 'y' VERB MENU AND NOT THE MINING SKILL. Both reach the same function.
# The verb menu is used here because it is deterministic: Player::YuseMenu asks
# Q_DIR, EffectPrompt answers a direction by setting e.EDir and NOT e.EXVal or
# e.EYVal, and Creature::Dig reads e.EXVal/e.EYVal -- which e.Clear() left at
# (0,0). So this dig always lands on map square (0,0), which is Indestructable
# Rock, whose MaterialHardness for AD_PIERCE is -1. -1 is not greater than 0, so
# the "That area is too hard" gate passes on any seed. (That mis-aimed target is
# a second defect and is NOT what this script is about.)
#
# The in-play route reaches the same division: wield the pickaxe, use the Mining
# skill, walk into a wall of solid igneous rock -- material MAT_MAGMA, hardness
# -1 for piercing -- which src/MakeLev.cpp:2153 writes around every magma,
# brimstone or igneous floor. That route needs the right region to generate, so
# it is not what a check should depend on.
#
# WHAT TO READ OFF THE LAST SCREEN. `percent = 100 / SkillLevel(SK_MINING)` and
# Skills.cpp prints max(0, 100 - m->PercentSI) when the dig finishes:
#
#   before the guard   "(100% structural integrity remaining.)"  AArch64 SDIV
#                      answers a zero divisor with 0, so nothing was spent
#   after  the guard   "(0% structural integrity remaining.)"    100/max(1,0)
#
# On x86 there is no "before": IDIV raises #DE and the process dies.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Gnome"
@choose "Gnome (Standard)"
@choose "Warrior"

p       # Abort to Point Buy; every attribute starts at 8, with 75 points
        # STR 9, DEX 18, CON 18, INT 18, WIS 5, CHA 18, LUC 17 == exactly 75
RIGHT DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN LEFT*3 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*9
ENTER
y       # Are these your final stats? -- yes

@choose "Neutral"
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat
a       # Focus on which weapon

# Skill Manager. Nine ranks, spent on the first five rows -- Athletics, Bluff,
# Climb, Craft, Find Weakness. Mining is far below them in the list and MUST NOT
# receive a rank; one rank in it makes this script measure nothing.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

@while "wish to worship" y
@choose "The Disciplined Expert"

ESC     # the keystroke that lands in the dungeon

# Move the pickaxe from the right shoulder into the weapon hand. Creature::Dig
# tests InSlot(SL_WEAPON), so carrying it is not enough.
i
f
SPACE
b
SPACE
f
SPACE
@dump:wielded
ESC

y
@choose "Dig"
i
@choose "pickaxe"
UP
@dump:digresult

@quit
